WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
Right after the Startup Venezuela Summit,

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:07.400
we went straight to Platanus Hack 2026,

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.250
Caracas.

4
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:13.490
This year Platanus run its hackathon as a tour of Latin

5
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:19.410
America, and my team and I got into the Caracas edition.

6
00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:24.020
We applied with our developer profiles,

7
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.200
the same team as last year's Alegría hackathon,

8
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.000
and not as Tripea.

9
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.800
As Tripialo or Sálvalo or Sálvalo or Sálvalo,

10
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.230
but each with our own technical profile.

11
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.960
It was funny because literally a year after the Alegría

12
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:50.120
2025 hackathon, we were back in Yummy's offices for

13
00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.190
another hackathon, only this time much tougher on the

14
00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:55.260
technical side.

15
00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:02.690
We built 3D, which turns an ordinary video of a person

16
00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.640
into movement data for robots.

17
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:11.040
A simulated robot learns to move on its own by imitating

18
00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.260
you, just like in real steel.

19
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.260
It works like this.

20
00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:21.960
You take any video, the movement is tracked and brought

21
00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.680
into a physics simulation.

22
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.780
The robot learns to move by itself across different

23
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:36.440
terrains and conditions, and the simulation data and the

24
00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:40.660
training model are exported in formats ready for

25
00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.260
hardware.

26
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:47.340
We built it on the premise that robotics and AI is the

27
00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.050
New Sexy.

28
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:57.800
We slept little, but what I learned at Alegría and all

29
00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:02.350
the mental work I put in helped me a lot at this

30
00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.260
hackathon.

31
00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.280
And not just me.

32
00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.260
The rest of the team, who are honestly really cool and

33
00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:09.460
good.

34
00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:13.260
We were all very locked in.

35
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:18.260
There were unlimited snacks, so I kept myself awake,

36
00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:21.260
