37
00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.260
We were all very much better.

38
00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:25.300
Our mentor was Sebastian Alcalá,

39
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:30.510
a product engineer at Yummy and a co-founder of Wink.

40
00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.260
We didn't win, but the level was impressive.

41
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:39.780
I had watched the videos of the past editions in Buenos

42
00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:44.730
Aires, Mexico and Bogotá, and Caracas truly lived up to

43
00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:45.260
them.

44
00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.260
The winner had a really cool 3D product.

45
00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:53.260
And although we lost, we learned too much.

46
00:02:53.260 --> 00:03:02.570
A fun fact is that our workspace was right next to

47
00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:08.030
Platanus Hack Arcade, the one I made the game space

48
00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:09.080
explorer for.

49
00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:14.480
So several times while we were focused on 3D,

50
00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.270
